\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The four-dimensional lattice comparison}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Fukaya and coauthors express the lattice index through half the signed spectral asymmetry of a massive Hermitian Wilson operator (\citet{p. 3, Eq. (4)}{fukaya2020lattice}). Their sign convention is #{-\eta /2}, where #{\eta=\nu_+-\nu_-} at a regular field. For a periodic four-dimensional lattice their mass profile places two interfaces perpendicular to the fourth axis (\citet{p. 4, Eq. (7)}{fukaya2020lattice}).}

\p{Their Eq. (8) records that the finite sign count is constant while no eigenvalue crosses zero. Their comparison with the curvature integral and the two boundary eta invariants uses a perturbative continuum analysis with specified mass scales (\citet{p. 5, Eqs. (8)-(9)}{fukaya2020lattice}). The finite two-dimensional [wall half-signature](fdip-01B3) has the exact nonlocal dependence in \ref{fdip-01B7}.}
